\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Come on, my partners In distress,
\par My comrades through the wilderness,
\par Who still your bodies feel;
\par Awhile forget your griefs and fears,
\par And look beyond this vale of tears
\par To that celestial hill.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Beyond the bounds of time and space,
\par Look foward to that  heavenly place,
\par The saints' secure abode:
\par On faith's strong eagle-pinions rise,
\par And force your passage to the skies,
\par And scale the mount of God.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Who suffer with our Master here,
\par We shall before His face appear,
\par And by His side 
\par sit down;
\par To patient faith the prize is sure,
\par The Cross, shall wear the crown.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Thrice blessed, bliss-inspiring hope!
\par It lifts the fainting spirits up,
\par It brings to life the dead;
\par Our conflicts here shall soon be past,
\par And you and I ascend at last,
\par Triumphant with our Head.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. That great mysterious Deity
\par We soon with open face shall see;
\par The beatific sight
\par Shall fill heaven's sounding courts with praise,
\par And wide diifuse the golden blaze
\par Of everlasting light.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. The Father shining on His throne,
\par The glorious co- eternal Son,
\par The Spirit, one and seven,
\par Conspire our rapture to complete;
\par And lo! we fall before His feet,
\par And silence heightens heaven.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. In hope of that ecstatic pause,
\par Jesus, we now sustain the cross
\par And at Thy footstool fall;
\par Till Thou our hidden life reveal,
\par Till Thou our ravished spirits fill,
\par And God is all in all.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

